{"variant": "compliance", "year": 1993, "month": 1, "day": 13, "slug": "vendor-contract-renewal-3345", "variant_int": 1, "html": "<section class=\"page-banner\"><div class=\"container\"><p class=\"text-uppercase mb-1\" style=\"color:var(--gold);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.75rem\"><a href=\"/archive/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">Archive</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1993/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">1993</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1993/01/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">01</a> &rsaquo; 13</p><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase\">Compliance Review &bull; CIS-1993-Q1-9189</p><h1 style=\"font-size:clamp(1.2rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.25\">Ethics &amp; Conduct Investigation Summary — Vendor Contract Renewal</h1><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:0\">State Government &bull; Executive Compensation Research Institute &bull; Archived 1993-01-13</p></div></section><section style=\"padding:3rem 0;background:var(--surface)\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"row g-4\"><div class=\"col-lg-8\"><div id=\"acpwb-compliance-9b9ef0a2-header\" style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:4px solid var(--gold);padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem\">Document Information</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.3rem .8rem;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem\"><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Client</span><br><strong>Executive Compensation Research Institute</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Industry</span><br><strong>State Government</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Audit Ref</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">CIS-1993-Q1-9189</code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Version</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">0.9-DRAFT</code></div></div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\">Filed by <strong>Bogdan Mccarthy</strong>, Senior Consultant, Athletic Compensation Advisory &mdash; <a href=\"mailto:bogdan.mccarthy@acpwb.com\" style=\"color:var(--navy)\">bogdan.mccarthy@acpwb.com</a></div><div style=\"margin-top:.6rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">Germany Corporate Governance Code (Deutscher Corporate Governance Kodex)</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">FLSA §207 (overtime provisions)</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">ERISA §404(c) (plan fiduciary standards)</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">1. Engagement Scope</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">Pursuant to the terms of the 1993 regulatory settlement agreement, ACPWB was engaged as an independent third-party monitor to assess Executive Compensation Research Institute&#x27;s compliance with the corrective action plan. This report covers the Q1 1993 review period and evaluates progress on 47 open remediation items.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">2. Methodology</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">The methodology for this review was aligned with the COSO Internal Control – Integrated Framework. Each of the 47 in-scope business processes was evaluated across the five COSO components: Control Environment, Risk Assessment, Control Activities, Information &amp; Communication, and Monitoring Activities.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">3. Findings Summary</h5><div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th>Finding ID</th><th>Risk</th><th>Status</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">CIS-1163-001</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">OPEN</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Vice President of Human Resources</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1993-02-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">OFCCP affirmative action plan goals not updated for the current plan year</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">CIS-9502-002</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">HIGH</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#dcfce7;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #86efac\">REMEDIATED</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Director of Workforce Development</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1993-03-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">NYSE/NASDAQ board independence requirements not met for 47 committee members</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">CIS-2286-003</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFO</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">OPEN</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Chief Strategy Officer</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1993-02-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Meal and rest break premiums not paid for 47 non-exempt employees with missed breaks in 4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">CIS-8357-004</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">OPEN</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Operations Coordinator</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1993-04-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Final pay for 47 terminated employees in California not provided within the statutory timeframe</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">4. Detailed Findings</h5><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">CIS-1163-001</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">OFCCP affirmative action plan goals not updated for the current plan year</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Immediately cease all inquiries into candidate salary history during the hiring process. Update all recruiter training materials and interview guides to reflect this prohibition.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">The identified control weakness has been contained through the implementation of a temporary manual workaround. A permanent, automated control is in development with a target implementation date of Q1 1994.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Vice President of Human Resources</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1993-02-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">CIS-9502-002</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">HIGH</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#dcfce7;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #86efac\">REMEDIATED</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">NYSE/NASDAQ board independence requirements not met for 47 committee members</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Executive Compensation Research Institute shall conduct a full pay equity analysis across all protected class segments within 45 days of report issuance and submit a remediation plan to ACPWB for review.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Management disputes the risk classification of this finding. While acknowledging the documentation gap, Executive Compensation Research Institute believes the underlying practices are compliant with applicable requirements. A formal response memorandum has been filed with the engagement team under separate cover.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Director of Workforce Development</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1993-03-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">CIS-2286-003</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFORMATIONAL</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Meal and rest break premiums not paid for 47 non-exempt employees with missed breaks in 4</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Automate the COBRA notification process to ensure qualifying event notices are generated and mailed within 5 business days of the triggering event.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Management agrees with the finding. The issue has been added to the agenda for the next quarterly business review with the responsible process owners to ensure accountability.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Chief Strategy Officer</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1993-02-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">CIS-8357-004</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Final pay for 47 terminated employees in California not provided within the statutory timeframe</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The deferred compensation plan committee will conduct a full review of all plan operations to ensure strict compliance with the documentary and operational requirements of IRC §409A.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">The finding is valid and has been added to our compliance remediation backlog. It has been prioritized for action in the next fiscal quarter, subject to resource availability.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Operations Coordinator</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1993-04-28</strong></div></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-top:1.5rem;padding-top:1.25rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><a href=\"/archive/1993/01/12/enterprise-architecture-review-board-decision-log-8700/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none\">